<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Latency Feed — token launch radar</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#board">Skip to the board</a>
<header class="top">
  <div>
    <h1>LATENCY FEED <span class="tag">token launch radar</span></h1>
    <p class="sub">The fastest signal on protocols whose token does not exist yet — ranked by implied value, with the farm plan for each one.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feed-meta">
    <div><span class="k">MODEL</span><span class="v" id="modelVer">—</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">SNAPSHOT</span><span class="v" id="snapDate">—</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">SOURCE</span><span class="v" id="snapSrc">—</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="stats" id="stats" aria-label="Feed totals"></section>

<section class="panel legend">
  <h2>How to read the feed</h2>
  <p><b>Implied value</b> = TVL × 0.30 × velocity × overdue × breadth. <b>Velocity</b> is the 7-day TVL change, clamped to −50…+150%. <b>Overdue</b> grows with the days a protocol has run with no token (up to 900 days). <b>Breadth</b> adds 4% per chain, up to 5 chains. <b>Signal age</b> is days from first listing to the snapshot date. Nothing here predicts whether or when a token is issued — it prices what the launch would be worth if the record stayed as it is.</p>
  <p class="badges"><span class="pill hot">HOT — daily velocity ≥ 1.5%: act within hours</span><span class="pill warm">WARM — 7-day change above zero: act within days</span><span class="pill cool">COOL — flat or falling: watch, no rush</span></p>
  <p class="fine">“Records no token” means the snapshot's record carries no market cap, CoinGecko id or symbol — not that the protocol has none. The watchlist is the floor, never the ceiling: the board ranks 200 early protocols below it too.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel controls" aria-label="Filter and sort">
  <label>Search <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="name or slug…" autocomplete="off"></label>
  <label>Chain <select id="chain"><option value="">All chains</option></select></label>
  <label>Category <select id="cat"><option value="">All categories</option></select></label>
  <label>Signal <select id="lat"><option value="">All signals</option><option value="hot">Hot only</option><option value="warm">Warm only</option><option value="cool">Cool only</option></select></label>
  <label>Min TVL <select id="minTvl"><option value="0">Any</option><option value="50000000">$50M+</option><option value="100000000">$100M+</option><option value="1000000000">$1B+</option></select></label>
